QPlayer standalone browser host

Backend source: ca.weblite/webview (swingwebview) 1.10.0
https://github.com/webliteca/swingwebview/tree/e4204268e5cdb4b51c6b5e093a8a591d96e56acc
Tag: v1.10.0; commit: e4204268e5cdb4b51c6b5e093a8a591d96e56acc
Retrieved: 2026-10-27
License: MIT; original license retained in upstream/LICENSE and source headers.

Vendored files retain the original WebKitGTK/WKWebView/WebView2 engine and
native cookie-store implementations. Local modifications expose standalone
GTK windows while retaining native input methods, add ephemeral WebKitGTK
contexts and WKWebsiteDataStore, add standalone WebView2 HWND/profile ownership,
fix the extra WebView2 reference and apartment cleanup, and make legacy JAWT
symbol resolution optional (no JAWT library is linked or loaded by this host).
qplayer_webview.cpp adapts these engines to a small Swing-free JNI API. No Java
sources from the upstream Swing component or dispatcher layer are shipped.

Build requirements:
- JDK headers via JAVA_HOME; CMake >= 3.20, C++17 compiler.
- Linux: pkg-config, GTK3, X11 and WebKitGTK 4.1 or 4.0 development headers.
  Runtime WebKitGTK/JavaScriptCore/libsoup are resolved by the upstream loader.
  Debian/Ubuntu: libgtk-3-dev libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev libx11-dev.
- macOS: Xcode command-line tools, Cocoa/WebKit/QuartzCore/Security frameworks;
  Objective-C++ and blocks. GLFW must continue to pump AppKit on the main thread.
- Windows: VS C++ tools and unpacked Microsoft.Web.WebView2 1.0.2592.51 SDK:
  https://www.nuget.org/api/v2/package/Microsoft.Web.WebView2/1.0.2592.51
  Pass -DWEBVIEW2_SDK=<SDK root>. The SDK's WebView2LoaderStatic.lib is linked;
  its Microsoft license applies. Runtime requires the installed WebView2 Runtime.
  SDK binaries are downloaded at build time, not vendored here.

Build from repository root (INSTALL_ROOT must be an absolute path):
  cmake -S desktop-host/native/webview -B desktop-host/target/webview-native \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=<INSTALL_ROOT>
  cmake --build desktop-host/target/webview-native --config Release
  cmake --install desktop-host/target/webview-native --config Release
Set INSTALL_ROOT to desktop-host/target/classes before Maven packages resources.
The install writes native-webview/{libqplayerwebview.so,libqplayerwebview.dylib,
qplayerwebview.dll} for the current platform and Native Image JNI/resource
metadata under META-INF/native-image/dev.t1m3.qplayer/webview.
Also copy this NOTICE and upstream/LICENSE to distribution notices.

JNI API: dev.t1m3.qplayer.desktop.app.DesktopNativeBrowser native methods
create/navigate/evaluate/cookies/isOpen/focus/destroy. Native callbacks are
DesktopNativeBrowser$Bridge.invoke(String,long) and
DesktopNativeBrowser$CookieReply.completed(String,String). No reflection-based
browser APIs, dynamic class generation, AWT event dispatch or JVM subprocess.
DesktopNativeBrowser and its nested Library must initialize at runtime in
Native Image; they create executors and extract/load the native resource.

Smoke scenarios for the integrated host (not run by this change):
- Official HTTPS login, HttpOnly credential cookie scoped to the configured URL;
  close/cancel, repeated open/focus, reopen with no previous account cookie.
- Native window resize, HiDPI and CJK input; login redirects and native dialogs.
- Hidden plugin JS: same-origin XHR/fetch, qplayerWebAuthDone, null result,
  thrown script, cancellation, 45-second timeout, redirect to a different origin.
- Close while cookie/eval callbacks are pending, and exit with either session
  active; no leftover browser windows/processes/profile directories.
- Windows: WebView2 unavailable, fresh independent profiles for overlapping
  login/script sessions, and successful profile removal after controller close.
- Native Image: run without a JDK/JRE, no java.desktop/Swing classes loaded;
  JNI callbacks and native libraries available on Linux/macOS/Windows.
